    <!-- ── Tiers ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="ts-section ts-section--white" id="tiers">
      <div class="tla-container">
        <div class="tla-section-header tla-fade">
          <span class="tla-overline">Four tiers</span>
          <h2>One size for every room</h2>
          <p>
            Instap is the pilot you start with. Station stands in the middle of the room. Tafel and Tafel XL are furniture with a screen in them rather than a monitor on a bracket &mdash; and that choice is about the size of the room, not the budget. Which one is right depends on your space and your light, so tell us about the room and we will say which we would put in it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every quote is the same four lines, and we show you all of them: the technology at close to what it costs us on the day, the part we build by hand, the licence, and a capped installation figure. No bundled line that hides where the money went.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ts-tiers-wrap">
        <div class="ts-tiers">
          {tiers.map((t, i) => (
            <article class={`ts-tier tla-fade${i ? ` tla-d${Math.min(i, 3)}` : ""}`}>
              <figure class="ts-tier__art">
                {art[t.id].map((a, j) => (
                  <img src={a.src} alt={a.alt} loading="lazy" hidden={j > 0} />
                ))}
                {art[t.id].length > 1 && (
                  <div class="ts-tier__switch">
                    {art[t.id].map((a, j) => (
                      <button type="button" aria-pressed={j === 0 ? "true" : "false"}>{a.label}</button>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                )}
              </figure>
              <div class="ts-tier__body">
                <h3 class="ts-tier__name">{t.name}</h3>
                <div class="ts-tier__size" set:html={t.size} />

                <div class="ts-tier__price">
                  <span set:html={t.totalEx.replace(/^(from|vanaf) /, '<small>$1</small> ')} />
                  <small>excl. VAT</small>
                </div>
                <div class="ts-tier__incl" set:html={`${t.totalIncl} incl. VAT`} />

                <details class="ts-breakdown">
                  <summary>What the price is made of</summary>
                  <ul class="ts-lines">
                    {t.lines.map((l) => (
                      <li class={l.craft ? "is-craft" : undefined}>
                        <span set:html={l.k} />
                        <strong set:html={l.v} />
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                </details>

                <div class="ts-tier__plus">
                  <span class="ts-label">Strong points</span>
                  <ul>
                    {t.plus.map((p) => <li set:html={p} />)}
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="ts-tier__sat">
                  <span class="ts-label">Satellite, same site</span>
                  <span set:html={t.satellite} />
                </div>

                {showCosts && (
                  <details class="ts-cost">
                    <summary>Cost and build &mdash; internal</summary>
                    <div class="ts-cost__inner">
                      <ul class="ts-cost__rows">
                        {t.bom.map((b) => (
                          <li><span set:html={b.k} /><strong set:html={b.v} /></li>
                        ))}
                        <li class="is-total"><span>Hardware cost</span><strong set:html={t.parts} /></li>
                      </ul>
                      <div class="ts-cost__hours">
                        Build: <strong>{t.hours} h</strong> <span set:html={`&mdash; labour value ${t.labour}`} /><br />
                        At cost: <strong set:html={`${t.parts} + ${t.hours} h`} />
                      </div>
                      <ul class="ts-cost__rows" style="margin-top:12px;">
                        <li><span>Hardware line on quote</span><strong set:html={t.hwLine} /></li>
                        <li><span>Licence + commissioning</span><strong set:html={t.services} /></li>
                      </ul>
                      <p class="ts-cost__note">
                        Build hours are repeat-build estimates. The first table of any size is a prototype and will run longer.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </details>
                )}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Ways to pay less ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="ts-section ts-section--alt" id="variants">
      <div class="tla-container">
        <div class="tla-section-header tla-fade">
          <span class="tla-overline">If the budget is the obstacle</span>
          <h2>Two ways to make it cost less</h2>
          <p>
            Neither of these is a stripped-down version. You get the same platform, the same apps and the same table &mdash; you simply supply more of it yourself. Ask about both before you decide the answer is no.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-variants">
          <div class="ts-variant tla-fade">
            <div class="ts-variant__name">Bring your own table</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__amount">&minus; &euro; 300 to &euro; 450</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__scope">On Tafel and Tafel XL</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__what">
              Your museum almost certainly owns a better table than a second-hand shop does &mdash; and one with a story attached to it. Supply it and we build into it. The steel subframe, the toughened glass, the ventilation and the fitting are still ours.
            </div>
            <p class="ts-variant__note">
              Comes off the bespoke table build line. The subframe stays with us &mdash; it carries the panel, and on the 55&quot; it carries the load.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ts-variant tla-fade tla-d1">
            <div class="ts-variant__name">Buy the hardware yourself</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__amount">&minus; approx. &euro; 350 to &euro; 2,580</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__scope">On every tier &mdash; more on the larger screens</div>
            <div class="ts-variant__what">
              We give you the exact part list. You buy the panel and the mini PC &mdash; or have them sponsored or donated, which happens more often than you would think. We charge &euro; 350 to advise, configure and integrate, and you own the hardware and its warranty outright.
            </div>
            <p class="ts-variant__note">
              The technology line comes off the quote and &euro; 350 goes back on. It costs us very little, because our margin was never in the box &mdash; which is why we can offer this and a hardware supplier cannot.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-stack tla-fade">
          <span class="ts-label">They stack</span>
          <ul class="ts-stack__rows">
            <li><span>Tafel XL, 55&quot; &mdash; excl. VAT</span><strong>from &euro; 7,000</strong></li>
            <li><span>Your own table</span><strong>&minus; &euro; 450</strong></li>
            <li><span>Your own hardware</span><strong>&minus; approx. &euro; 2,580</strong></li>
            <li class="is-total"><span>What you pay us</span><strong>&euro; 3,970 <small>&euro; 4,804 incl. VAT</small></strong></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="ts-stack__note">
            Plus the panel and mini PC you buy yourself &mdash; about &euro; 2,300 at the prices we pay. A 55&quot; bespoke touch table, and the hardware is yours.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Comparison ─────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="ts-section ts-section--white" id="compare">
      <div class="tla-container">
        <div class="tla-section-header tla-fade">
          <span class="tla-overline">Side by side</span>
          <h2>What actually differs</h2>
          <p>
            Brightness, surface area and the physical size of the interface are the real differences. Pixel density is not &mdash; on the tables you are buying surface, not sharpness.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ts-tablewrap tla-fade">
          <table class="ts-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Specification</th>
                {tiers.map((t) => <th scope="col">{t.name}</th>)}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {compare.map((r) => (
